{{Quote|Heeded my words not, did you? Pass on what you have learned. Strength, mastery. But weakness&hellip; folly&hellip; failure, also. Yes, failure most of all. The greatest teacher, failure is. Luke&hellip; we are what they grow beyond. That is the true burden of all masters.|Yoda's Force spirit, to Luke Skywalker|<ref name="Episode 8">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>}}
'''Jedi Master''' was a rank in the [[Jedi Order]] given to wise and powerful [[Jedi]], many of whom were prominent leaders within the Order.

Only Masters were allowed to serve on the [[Jedi High Council]]. A notable exception to this, however, was when [[Anakin Skywalker]] was appointed to the Council as a representative of [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] despite only being a [[Jedi Knight]].

==Description==
{{Quote|Those who have undertaken the most serious study and hold the deepest devotion to the Force will achieve the rank of Jedi Master. It is more than just an honorary title, for upon achieving the rank of Master, the Order expects a Jedi to forge their own path and pursue independent studies. However, some masters might still take a Padawan, or return to the Grand Temple to educate younglings. Masters are also eligible to be named to the Grand Council as leaders of the Order. For a very select few, the title of Grand Master awaits only the most illustrious among us.|Jedi Master [[Harli Cogra]]|<ref name="Chronicles of the Jedi">''[[Star Wars: The High Republic: Chronicles of the Jedi]]''</ref>}}
[[File:Yoda_ME.png|thumb|left|250px|Yoda was both a Jedi Master and Grand Master of the Jedi Order.]]
A [[Jedi]] Master was a [[Jedi Knight]] who had been offered a higher ranking within [[Jedi Order]] as a result of a Jedi [[Grand Master]] seeing the Knight fit for the position.<ref name="TSWB" /> Compared to a Knight, a Jedi Master had greater experience, greater readiness, and had shown their devotion to taking their next step as part of the Order: to be a Jedi Master was the next rank all Jedi Knights worked towards as part of their life-long devotion to studying [[The Force]], but it was a long road to prove oneself worthy of the title.<ref name="Convergence">''[[The High Republic: Convergence]]''</ref> Upon being given the rank, the Jedi Master was able to and expected to pursue their own studies, moving forward in their experience with [[the Force]] on their own terms. In fact, the [[Jedi High Council]] outright expected all Jedi Masters to do so.<ref name="Light of the Jedi">''[[The High Republic: Light of the Jedi]]''</ref>

There were several ways for a Jedi Knight to be promoted into a Jedi Master. One way was for the Knight to successfully train [[Padawan]]s, passing on their knowledge of [[the Force]]<ref name="Insider 199">{{InsiderCite|199|A Seat on the Council}}</ref> in order to ensure the Order survived into the next generation.<ref name="TCWFilm" /> Alternatively, a Jedi Knight could prove themself in battle.<ref name="Insider 199" /> In general, those who were offered the rank of Master had undertaken serious study and held a deep loyalty to the Force.<ref name="Chronicles of the Jedi" /> When the moment called for a serious response, Jedi Masters were expected to be serious instead of acting glib.<ref name="Kanan 7">[[Kanan 7|''Kanan'' 7]]</ref> Often groups of [[Jedi Initiate|Jedi younglings]] would receive their early education in the ways of the Force under the guidance of a single Jedi Master. The [[youngling]]s would then receive more direct [[Jedi training|training]] under the direction from either a Jedi Knight or a Jedi Master.<ref name="TSWB" /> Jedi Masters and Jedi Knights served as Jedi Generals in the [[Republic Military]] during the [[Clone Wars]] while [[Padawan]]s served as [[Jedi Commander]]s.<ref name="TCWFilm" />

==History==
{{Quote|The title of Jedi Master was bestowed upon the most powerful members of the Jedi Order.|Luke Skywalker|<ref name="Star Wars: The Secrets of the Jedi">''[[Star Wars: The Secrets of the Jedi]]''</ref>}}
[[File:KelleranBeqBalance-ABig.png|thumb|right|250px|Jedi Master [[Kelleran Beq]]]]
In the time of the [[High Republic Era|High Republic]], the Jedi High Council notably consisted of three Jedi Grand Masters; [[Xo Lahru]], [[Pra-Tre Veter]], and [[Yoda]] all elected to share the role. Other masters of High [[Republic Era]] included [[Jora Malli]], [[Stellan Gios]], [[Sskeer]], [[Oppo Rancisis]], [[Yarael Poof]], and [[Avar Kriss]].<ref name="Light of the Jedi" /> [[Ry Ki-Sakka]] also gained the Grand Master rank at some point.<ref name="THRS 4">{{HighRepublicShow|xqBuS4EZ0qE|High Republic Jedi Council Deep Dive, a Lesson on Wayseekers, and More!|sw_url=video/high-republic-jedi-council-deep-dive-a-lesson-on-wayseekers-and-more}}</ref> As one of the oldest Jedi Masters in the order's history, Yoda,<ref name="Episode V">{{Film|V}}</ref> over the course of his 800-[[Standard year|year]]-long career as a Jedi Master, trained no fewer than 20,000 Jedi<ref name="AEYTK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> and held the position of Jedi Grand Master for over 800 years.<ref name="DatabankYoda">{{Databank|yoda|Yoda}}</ref>

In the years of the [[Galactic Republic]], the Jedi High Council was made up of twelve Jedi Masters, one which bore the title of Grand Master,<ref name="sweJO">{{SWE|groups|jediorder|Jedi Order}}</ref> who had the power to grant Jedi Knights the title of Master, in consensus. Other prominent Jedi Masters who also sat on the Council included members, such as [[Mace Windu]], [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], [[Kit Fisto]], [[Adi Gallia]], [[Yaddle]], [[Saesee Tiin]], [[Agen Kolar]], [[Even Piell]], and [[Shaak Ti]].<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> Many Jedi Masters also took on apprentices to train in the ways of the Force, such as [[Depa Billaba]]<ref name="A New Dawn">[[A New Dawn (novel)|''A New Dawn'']]</ref> and [[Luminara Unduli]].<ref name="Weapons Factory">{{TCW|Weapons Factory}}</ref>

[[File:Wolfpack_Felucia.png|thumb|left|300px|During the Clone Wars, Jedi Masters held the rank of Jedi General over clone troopers in the Republic Military.]]
Under the [[Jedi Military Integration Act]], Jedi Masters and Jedi Knights were given the rank of Jedi General for the Clone Wars.<ref name="Brotherhood">[[Brotherhood (novel)|''Brotherhood'']]</ref> After serving as a Jedi Knight for three years during the war, [[Anakin Skywalker]] advanced to the point in his training that he felt he deserved the rank of Jedi Master, though the Council did not agree. When [[Supreme Chancellor]] [[Darth Sidious|Sheev Palpatine]] appointed Skywalker to the Council as his personal representative, the Council reluctantly agreed, hoping to use him as a means to [[spy]] on Palpatine. However, the Council did not grant Skywalker the title of Master. Skywalker took this as both an outrageous and unfair insult, as no Jedi in the history of the Jedi Order had ever been placed on the Council without receiving the rank of Master.<ref name="Episode III" />

Years after the [[Great Jedi Purge]] and the [[Galactic Civil War]], [[Luke Skywalker]] attempted to train his own generation of Jedi and was considered a Jedi Master.<ref name="Episode VII">{{Film|VII}}</ref><ref>''[[The Secrets of the Jedi]]''</ref> Following the [[Battle of Exegol]] in [[35 ABY]],<ref name="TROS Date">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]'' dates the events of ''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'' as taking place one [[Standard year|year]] after the [[Hosnian Cataclysm|Starkiller Incident]], which ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'' dates to [[34 ABY]]. Therefore, the events of ''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'' must take place in [[35 ABY]].</ref> [[Rey Skywalker|Rey]] took up the [[Skywalker family|family name]] of her mentors Luke Skywalker and<ref name="TSWB" /> [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo]].<ref name="TROS EE">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: Expanded Edition]]''</ref> Now the last Jedi, Rey Skywalker eventually ascended to the rank of Master.<ref name="TSWB" />

==Behind the scenes==
As confirmed by editor [[Tom Hoeler]], the word "master" in "Jedi Master" must be capitalized if used with "Jedi." The word "master" on its own, however, does not always need to be capitalized.<ref name="Jedi Master Tom">{{Twitter|DarthInternous|status/1770107828499271783|[[Tom Hoeler]]|quote=Master should always be capitalized when used in combination with the word Jedi. Master on its own does not always require capitalization.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/j92WB}}</ref> "Master Jedi," meanwhile, is an honorific used among certain cultures or by certain individuals, rather than a reference to the "Jedi Master" rank itself.<ref name="Jedi Master Tom 2">{{Twitter|DarthInternous|status/1770313258920038481|[[Tom Hoeler]]|quote=Jedi is a singular plural, so Jedi is always Jedi. Master Jedi is usually an honorific used by certain beings and cultures, and as such would be capitalized because it is a referrant. {{C|In response to: "But should it be Master Jedis or Jedi masters?"}}|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/TD7RO}}</ref>

